Notebook[{Cell["Lepton-quark scattering, step 5: the double-longitudinal NLO \
hard coefficient", "Title"], Cell["Same structure as 4-Unpolarized.wl (read \
that first), for the helicity difference Delta sigma = (sigma(++) - \
sigma(+-))/2 of the incoming lepton and quark.  Input: \
Results/<route>/Algebra.wl and Reduced.wl.  Output: \
Results/<route>/Polarized.wl and the comparison with Hinderer, Schlegel and \
Vogelsang, arXiv:1703.10872.\n\nThree things differ from the unpolarized \
case.  (1) The HVBM scheme: the polarized matrix elements of step 2 contain \
the hatted invariant spe3, which step 3 turned into integrals in D + 2 \
dimensions; they are already included in reduced[\"Real\"][\"Polarized\"].  \
(2) The splitting functions: the incoming quark and the photon in the lepton \
are polarized, Delta Pqq = Pqq and Delta P_photon/lepton(y) = 2 - y; the \
outgoing quark fragments unpolarized.  (3) The HVBM scheme breaks helicity \
conservation at the quark-gluon vertex by a finite amount; the standard \
remedy (Ref. Vogelsang 1996, used in arXiv:1703.10872) is a finite \
renormalization of the polarized quark density with the kernel Delta f_qq = \
-4 CF (1-z), i.e. the hard part receives the additional term -(alphaS/(2 Pi)) \
Delta f_qq (x) Delta sigma_Born.\n\nAll factorization scales (incoming quark, \
outgoing quark, photon in lepton) are set equal to muR, as in that paper.", 
   "Text"], Cell["Load", "Section"], Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirector\
y[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["route = \"FeynCalc\";\nalgebra = LoadResult[\"Algebra\", \
route];\nreduced = LoadResult[\"Reduced\", route];\nregion = s > 0 && muR > 0 \
&& 0 < v < 1 && 0 < w < 1;\ntoVW = {t -> -s (1 - v), s4 -> s v (1 - w), u -> \
-s v w};\ncouplings = {ee -> Sqrt[4 Pi alphaEM], gs -> Sqrt[4 Pi \
alphaS]};\nKeys[reduced]", "Input"], Cell["Born terms", "Section"], 
  Cell["The polarized Born square has no order-eps term; born0 = 2 alphaEM^2 \
eq^2 (1+v)/(s v (1-v)).", "Text"], Cell["bornHard = \
Series[algebra[\"Born\"][\"Polarized\"]/(16 Pi^2 s v) /. D -> 4 - 2 eps /. \
couplings /. {t -> -s (1 - v), u -> -s v}, {eps, 0, 1}];\nborn0 = \
SeriesCoefficient[bornHard, {eps, 0, 0}] // Simplify;\nborn1 = \
SeriesCoefficient[bornHard, {eps, 0, 1}] // Simplify;\nRequire[Simplify[born0 \
- 2 alphaEM^2 eq^2 (1 + v)/(s v (1 - v))] === 0, \"Polarized Born hard part \
differs from the expected form\"];\n{born0, born1}", "Input"], 
  Cell["Polarized photon-quark Born, normalized as in the unpolarized case; \
its order-eps part (the evanescent term of the HVBM scheme) enters the finite \
photon-in-lepton subtraction.", "Text"], Cell["yPhoton = (1 - v)/(1 - v \
w);\nphotonHard = Series[(Pi/alphaS) algebra[\"Photon\"][\"Polarized\"]/(16 \
Pi^2 yPhoton s (1 - v w)) /. D -> 4 - 2 eps /. couplings /.\n  {sh -> yPhoton \
s, th -> -s (1 - v), uh -> -yPhoton s v w}, {eps, 0, 1}];\nphoton0 = \
Simplify[SeriesCoefficient[photonHard, {eps, 0, 0}], region];\nphoton1 = \
Simplify[SeriesCoefficient[photonHard, {eps, 0, 1}], region];\n{photon0, \
photon1}", "Input"], Cell["Real emission and its threshold expansion", 
   "Section"], Cell["As in the unpolarized case: the exact threshold factors \
s4^(-eps), zAB^(-1-eps) and zAB^(-eps) give the branches (1-w)^(-1-2eps) and \
(1-w)^(-1-eps); ThresholdSplit separates them and EndpointExpand turns each \
into plus distributions.  The polarized result includes the dimension-shifted \
(D+2) masters of the hatted terms.", "Text"], Cell["realHard = muR^(2 eps) \
reduced[\"Real\"][\"Polarized\"]/(32 Pi^3) /. couplings /. toVW;\nsplit = \
ThresholdSplit[realHard, w, eps];\nKeys[split[\"Branches\"]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["EndpointExpand applies (1-w)^(-1-lambda eps) = -delta(1-w)/(lambda \
eps) + D0 - lambda eps D1 + ... to every branch, with D0 = [1/(1-w)]_+ and D1 \
= [log(1-w)/(1-w)]_+, and splits w-dependent coefficients into their value at \
w = 1 times the distribution plus an ordinary remainder.  The result has the \
double pole, the single poles in the basis {regular, D0, delta} and the \
finite part in {regular, D0, D1, delta}.", "Text"], 
  Cell["realExpanded = EndpointExpand[split[\"Regular\"], \
split[\"Branches\"], eps, w, region];\nSimplify[realExpanded[\"Pole2\"], \
region]", "Input"], Cell["Virtual correction", "Section"], 
  Cell["The vector form factor multiplies the polarized Born term; helicity \
is conserved at the photon vertex.", "Text"], 
  Cell["virtualHard = Series[alphaS CF/(2 Pi) (4 Pi muR^2)^eps \
reduced[\"Virtual\"] (born0 + eps born1) /. t -> -s (1 - v), {eps, 0, \
0}];\nvirtualHard = Map[Simplify[#, region] &, virtualHard];\nvirtualPole2 = \
SeriesCoefficient[virtualHard, {eps, 0, -2}];\nvirtualPole1 = \
SeriesCoefficient[virtualHard, {eps, 0, -1}];\nvirtualFinite = \
SeriesCoefficient[virtualHard, {eps, 0, \
0}];\nRequire[Simplify[realExpanded[\"Pole2\"] + virtualPole2, region] === 0, \
\"Double poles do not cancel\"];\n\"double poles cancel\"", "Input"], 
  Cell["Collinear counterterms and the single poles", "Section"], 
  Cell["As in the unpolarized case, with Delta Pqq(w)/w = CF [(1-w)/w + \
2/(1-w)]_+ + 3/2 delta(1-w) for the incoming polarized quark, the unpolarized \
Pqq for the fragmenting quark, and Delta P_photon/lepton(y) = 2 - y.", 
   "Text"], Cell["incomingTuple[bornTerm_] := CF bornTerm {(1 - w)/w, 2, \
3/2};\ndw = 1 - v + v w;\njFunction[bornTerm_] := v w (bornTerm /. v -> v \
w/dw)/dw^2;              (* Born at the shifted point, with the Jacobian \
*)\nfragmentation[j_] := Module[{jEnd = Simplify[j /. w -> 1, region]},\n  \
CF/v {2 (j - jEnd)/(1 - w) - v j (1 + dw), 2 jEnd, jEnd (2 Log[v] + \
3/2)}];\nphotonKernel = 2 - yPhoton;                                          \
        (* Delta P_photon/lepton *)\npdfPole = alphaS/(2 Pi) \
incomingTuple[born0];\nffPole = alphaS/(2 Pi) \
fragmentation[jFunction[born0]];\nphotonPole = {alphaEM/(2 Pi) photonKernel \
alphaS/Pi photon0, 0, 0};\npoleTable = {realExpanded[\"Pole1\"], {0, 0, \
virtualPole1}, pdfPole, ffPole, photonPole};\nsinglePoles = \
Total[poleTable];\nRequire[And @@ (ExactDifference[#, 0, region] === 0 & /@ \
singlePoles), \"Single poles do not cancel\", \
singlePoles];\nGrid[Prepend[MapThread[Prepend[Map[Simplify[#, region] &, #2], \
#1] &,\n  {{\"real emission\", \"virtual\", \"incoming quark\", \"outgoing \
quark\", \"photon in lepton\", \"sum\"}, Append[poleTable, singlePoles]}],\n  \
{\"1/eps coefficient of\", \"regular\", \"D0\", \"delta\"}], Alignment -> \
Left, Dividers -> {{2 -> True}, {2 -> True, 7 -> True}}]", "Input"], 
  Cell["The finite hard coefficient", "Section"], 
  Cell["The regular parts still contain the inert symbols F1[n][zAB] etc. of \
the hypergeometric functions; they are replaced by their explicit expressions \
(logarithms and dilogarithms) here.  Finite parts of the counterterms as \
before, plus the helicity-restoring term -(alphaS/(2 Pi)) Delta f_qq (x) \
Delta sigma_Born with Delta f_qq(z) = -4 CF (1-z) on the incoming quark leg \
(HelicityRestorationKernel), which contributes +(alphaS/(2 Pi)) 4 CF (1-w)/w \
born0 to the regular part.", "Text"], Cell["pdfFinite = alphaS/(2 Pi) \
(MSbarConstant incomingTuple[born0] + incomingTuple[born1]);\nffFinite = \
alphaS/(2 Pi) (MSbarConstant fragmentation[jFunction[born0]] + \
fragmentation[jFunction[born1] + 2 jFunction[born0] Log[dw]]);\nphotonFinite \
= {alphaEM/(2 Pi) photonKernel alphaS/Pi (MSbarConstant photon0 + photon1), \
0, 0};\nhelicityRestoration = {-alphaS/(2 Pi) HelicityRestorationKernel[w]/w \
born0, 0, 0};\ncounterterms = {#[[1]], #[[2]], 0, #[[3]]} &[pdfFinite + \
ffFinite + photonFinite + helicityRestoration];\nfinite = \
realExpanded[\"Finite\"] + {0, 0, 0, virtualFinite} + \
counterterms;\nfiniteTable = {realExpanded[\"Finite\"], {0, 0, 0, \
virtualFinite}, {#[[1]], #[[2]], 0, #[[3]]} &[pdfFinite],\n  {#[[1]], #[[2]], \
0, #[[3]]} &[ffFinite], {#[[1]], #[[2]], 0, #[[3]]} &[photonFinite], {#[[1]], \
#[[2]], 0, #[[3]]} &[helicityRestoration]};\nfiniteNames = {\"real \
emission\", \"virtual\", \"incoming quark\", \"outgoing quark\", \"photon in \
lepton\", \"helicity restoration\"};\nfinite = finite /. \
reduced[\"MasterFunctions\"];                 (* insert the explicit F1, F2 \
functions *)\nprefactor = CF alphaEM^2 eq^2 alphaS/(Pi s v \
w);\nprefactorEndpoint = prefactor /. w -> 1;          (* the D0, D1 and \
delta coefficients are defined at w = 1 *)\ncoefficients = \
Map[Collect[Expand[#], {_Log, _PolyLog}, Factor] &,\n  finite/{prefactor, \
prefactorEndpoint, prefactorEndpoint, \
prefactorEndpoint}];\nTableForm[Transpose[{ThresholdBasis, coefficients}]]", 
   "Input"], Cell["The same coefficients split into their contributions (in \
units of the prefactor; regular parts with the explicit F1, F2 functions \
inserted):", "Text"], Cell["Grid[Prepend[MapThread[Prepend[Map[Simplify[#, \
region] &, #2 /. reduced[\"MasterFunctions\"]], #1] &,\n  {finiteNames, \
Map[#/{prefactor, prefactorEndpoint, prefactorEndpoint, prefactorEndpoint} &, \
finiteTable]}],\n  {\"finite part of\", \"regular\", \"D0\", \"D1\", \
\"delta\"}], Alignment -> Left, Dividers -> {{2 -> True}, {2 -> True}}]", 
   "Input"], Cell["Comparison with the literature", "Section"], 
  Cell["reference/HSV2017-polarized.wl transcribes the paper's result exactly \
as printed: its prefactor and its coefficients of 1, D0, D1 and delta(1-w).  \
The paper's prefactor contains 1/w and multiplies the distributions as well, \
so the two forms must be compared as distributions: CanonicalDistribution \
turns the paper's form into the basis used here with the identities f(w) D0 = \
f(1) D0 + (f(w) - f(1))/(1-w) and f(w) D1 = f(1) D1 + (f(w) - f(1)) \
log(1-w)/(1-w).  The difference must vanish identically in the physical \
region; it is also evaluated numerically at three points.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"reference\", \
\"HSV2017-polarized.wl\"}]];\npaper = HSV2017Polarized[s, v, w, muR, alphaEM, \
alphaS, eq, CF];\nliterature = CanonicalDistribution[paper[\"Prefactor\"], \
paper[\"Coefficients\"], w];\ndifference = Table[ExactDifference[finite[[i]], \
literature[[i]], region], {i, 4}];\nnumeric = NumericDifference[finite, \
literature, PhysicalPoints, 20];\n{difference, numeric}", "Input"], 
  Cell["Save", "Section"], Cell["The result is saved before the final check, \
so that a failed comparison still leaves every ingredient on disk for \
inspection.", "Text"], Cell["result = <|\"Basis\" -> ThresholdBasis, \
\"Prefactor\" -> prefactor, \"Coefficients\" -> coefficients, \"Finite\" -> \
finite,\n  \"Born\" -> born0, \"Virtual\" -> virtualFinite, \"Real\" -> \
realExpanded[\"Finite\"], \"Counterterms\" -> counterterms,\n  \
\"LiteratureDifference\" -> difference, \"Route\" -> \
route|>;\nSaveResult[\"Polarized\", result, route];\nRequire[difference === \
{0, 0, 0, 0}, \"Finite coefficient differs from HSV 2017\", \
difference];\ncoefficients[[4]]", "Input"]}, WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
